{{!
    @template block_compass/preload

    The modulepreload hints the top-of-body hook writes where the block is (ADR-011, decision 2
    and amendment 5): one link per module the client will import, so the browser fetches all of
    them while it parses these lines instead of discovering each level after the previous one
    arrived. At the top of the body and not in the head, because a module preload that precedes
    the import map makes the browser ignore the map.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * links - a list of objects with one key, href: the absolute URL of one module, the same
      URL the import map will contain a few lines later.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "links": [
            {"href": "https://example.com/esm/1/react"},
            {"href": "https://example.com/esm/1/@moodle/lms/block_compass/bundle"}
        ]
    }
}}
{{#links}}
<link rel="modulepreload" href="{{href}}">
{{/links}}
